  "title": "PoloHortiguela2025: Motor imagery of ankle dorsiflexion/plantarflexion dataset",
  "description": "Open-loop EEG dataset of kinesthetic motor imagery of ankle dorsiflexion/plantarflexion alternated with relaxation, recorded from six healthy participants. Each participant completed two sessions, one with a static and one with a moving lower-limb exoskeleton. Data were recorded with 28 EEG channels and 4 EOG channels at 250 Hz and re-released in BIDS format via MOABB.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded at 250 Hz from 28 EEG channels, 4 EOG channels and 3 miscellaneous channels, using a standard_1005 montage. Participants performed cue-based (auditory) kinesthetic motor imagery of ankle dorsiflexion/plantarflexion versus rest in 4 s trials, over 11 runs per session, in a static and a motion exoskeleton session.",
